  "companyID": "58c62e995865713647a7115d",
  "created": "2018-01-28T00:02:26.514Z",
  "deletedAt": null,
  "details": "Hey there! As someone who has a whole lot of worlds, and as someone who is also trying to promote membership in my main club world, I have a portal out to Club Transcendia in all of my new worlds. \n\nHowever, I've recently noticed that each portal in each room leads to a separate instance which actually does more to separate the traffic I am interested in directing rather than bringing people to one instance, and then switching over to another instance once that one gets full. \n\nI frequently see a ton of 1-2 person instances that I think may be a result of this. If instead all prefab portals directed traffic to one main instance until that one filled up, I think that would support growth rather than spreading it out over multiple lonely instances. \n\nThanks for considering this!\n\n- With Love, TheArchitect",
